      "writtenOn": "2024-10-07T16:18:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I just realized we never implemented `\"rkp-vm\"` as a formal type on the backend.\n\nDoes this pass tests? I expect it to, but before submitting I wanted to be super sure you had verified 😊",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 66,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 66,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "a4ad719ee92a55bbc5a16cb7d01109b104402206",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "735060ff_b81562de",
        "filename": "libs/libservice_vm_requests/src/rkp.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 66,
      "author": {
        "id": 1958315
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-08T07:55:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I just realized we never implemented \"rkp-vm\" \n\nI also just realized that this value is not used anywhere...\n\nI checked that the test `VtsHalRemotelyProvisionedComponentTargetTest` passes without any issue. Mostly because the certificate type is not checked [1]. Are there any other RKP tests I should check?\n\nOtherwise, would you mind if I check in [1] that if it\u0027s avf then the value should be \"rkp-vm\"? Since the AVF HAL is purely android provided, we can enforce the value.\n\n[1] https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:hardware/interfaces/security/keymint/support/remote_prov_utils.cpp;l\u003d923;drc\u003de2346b7a13e3d04291a05763d9ba28e5d19180a9",
      "parentUuid": "25b58a2d_e9330a8d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 66,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 66,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "a4ad719ee92a55bbc5a16cb7d01109b104402206",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ea23e3bc_2ff3a9c4",
        "filename": "libs/libservice_vm_requests/src/rkp.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 66,
      "author": {
        "id": 1833664
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-08T16:31:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Technically, our spec does allow for custom certificate types: _\"Custom certificate types may be used, but the provisioning server may reject the request for an unknown certificate type.\"_\n\nSo we shouldn\u0027t start locking down certificate type. I think there\u0027s an argument for locking the field down to a finite set of values, but doing that is a larger discussion than I think we should have in an AOSP CL comment thread 😊\n\npackages/modules/RemoteKeyProvisioning/app/tests/avf/src/com/android/avf/rkpdapp/e2etest/AvfIntegrationTest.java is the critical test here.\n\nAs long as this test passes after changing certificate type to \"rkp-vm\", then we should be good to go.",
      "parentUuid": "735060ff_b81562de",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 66,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 66,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "a4ad719ee92a55bbc5a16cb7d01109b104402206",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
